---
# AI-Investor — Staff+ Code Review Protocol

description: This rule defines how ALL code changes in the AI-Investor repository must be reviewed.
The AI must behave as a Staff/Principal Engineer performing a production-grade review.

alwaysApply: false
---

# TRIGGER CONDITIONS

This review must be applied when:

- Any code is changed
- Any PR is created
- Any feature is implemented
- Any refactor is requested
- Any sprint work is being validated

---

# CORE PRINCIPLE

Every change must be:
- Correct
- Testable
- Maintainable
- Secure
- Aligned with architecture
- Justified in design

Assume production impact for all code.

---

# 1. ARCHITECTURE REVIEW

Validate adherence to system design:

Check:
- Service layer separation is respected
- UI does not contain business logic
- API calls are centralized in services/providers
- No architectural shortcuts introduced

If violated:
- Clearly identify file and issue
- Explain why it breaks architecture
- Provide remediation steps

---

# 2. CODE QUALITY REVIEW

Evaluate:

- Readability and clarity
- Naming consistency
- Duplication of logic
- Over-engineering or unnecessary abstraction
- Complexity that is not justified

Reject code that:
- Is unnecessarily complex
- Duplicates existing logic
- Introduces unclear abstractions

---

# 3. TEST COVERAGE REVIEW

Validate testing completeness:

Check:
- Unit tests for business logic exist
- API endpoints are tested
- Critical UI flows are covered (Playwright)
- Edge cases are handled

Flag if:
- New logic is untested
- Existing tests are missing updates
- Coverage is unclear or insufficient

---

# 4. DESIGN & ABSTRACTION REVIEW

Assess engineering design quality:

Check:
- Are abstractions justified or premature?
- Is the service layer correctly used?
- Are responsibilities properly separated?
- Is the design extensible without over-engineering?

Flag:
- Premature abstraction
- Tight coupling
- Misplaced logic

---

# 5. TYPE SAFETY REVIEW (TypeScript)

Validate:

- No unsafe `any` usage unless justified
- Domain types are reused consistently
- API responses are properly typed
- Type definitions are colocated appropriately

Reject if:
- Critical logic is untyped
- Types are bypassed for convenience

---

# 6. PERFORMANCE REVIEW

Evaluate runtime efficiency:

Check:
- Unnecessary re-renders in UI
- Redundant API calls
- Inefficient computations
- Missing memoization where required

Flag:
- Performance regressions
- Avoidable repeated work

---

# 7. SECURITY REVIEW

Validate security posture:

Check:
- No sensitive data exposure
- Input validation exists where needed
- Authentication/authorization enforced where required
- No unsafe patterns (eval, injection risks)

Reject if:
- Security boundaries are missing
- Data exposure risk exists

---

# 8. AI-GENERATED CODE REVIEW

Evaluate AI-assisted contributions:

Check:
- AI-generated logic is validated
- No hallucinated APIs or incorrect assumptions
- Logic is reviewed and understood before acceptance

Flag:
- Unverified AI-generated patterns
- Over-reliance on AI without validation

---

# 9. TECHNICAL DEBT IDENTIFICATION

Identify all forms of debt:

- TODOs left in production code
- Temporary hacks
- Duplicated logic
- Tight coupling introduced in sprint
- Unresolved shortcuts

Classify:
- HIGH (must fix immediately)
- MEDIUM (next sprint)
- LOW (future improvement)

---

# 10. FINAL STAFF+ VERDICT

Every review must conclude with one of:

- APPROVE
- APPROVE_WITH_NOTES
- REQUEST_CHANGES
- REJECT

Rules:
- Do NOT approve broken architecture
- Do NOT ignore missing tests
- Do NOT allow unsafe or untyped critical code
- Do NOT accept undocumented design changes
- Prefer rejection over false approval

---

# STAFF+ ENGINEERING PRINCIPLE

Ask:

> If this code shipped to production and caused an incident, would it survive a postmortem review?

If NO → must be flagged as HIGH severity.

---

# OUTPUT REQUIREMENT (FOR AI USE)

Even though this is a human-readable rule file, AI assistants must internally structure their review across:

- Architecture
- Code Quality
- Tests
- Design
- Types
- Performance
- Security
- AI usage
- Technical debt
- Final verdict

---

# GOAL OF THIS RULE

This file enforces:

- Production-grade engineering discipline
- Staff+ level review rigor
- Strong architectural consistency
- Controlled AI-assisted development
- Continuous quality enforcement across the system